$ whycant exec /srv/glibc-app

✗ alice (uid 1000) cannot exec /srv/glibc-app

  /                          drwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /srv                       drwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /srv/glibc-app             -rwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ exec
  /lib                       ·                      ✗ dynamic loader does not exist   ← blocked here
  /lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1   ·           not evaluated

Why
  /srv/glibc-app needs the dynamic loader /lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1, which does not exist. That is why running
  it fails with "No such file or directory" even though the file is there. It was
  probably built for another system, such as a glibc program on musl-based Alpine
  or the reverse.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Install the C library it was built against, or use a statically linked build.
